s construction fails.\n\nWe need to adjust slopes to cover all column 4 points.\n\nWe need three lines covering column 4 points (1,2,3). We have four lines total, but one line (the one covering column 6) may not need to cover column 4. So we need three of the remaining lines to have integer values at x=4 equal to 1,2,3 (distinct). So we need to assign slopes a_i for three lines such that v_i + a_i ∈ {1,2,3} distinct.\n\nWe have lines anchored at v_i = 1,2,3,4. We need to assign slopes a_i for three of them (maybe not all four) to satisfy this.\n\nLet's try to assign slopes for v_i=1,2,4 to cover column 4 points 1,2,3. Then the line with v_i=3 can be used for column 6 only.\n\nThus we need:\n\n- For line with v=1: a_1 such that 1 + a_1 = some value in {1,2,3}. Since a_1 cannot be 0 (horizontal), we need a_1 = 1 (to get 2) or a_1 = 2 (to get 3) or a_1 = 0 (to get 1) but 0 not allowed. So a_1 can be 1 (gives f(4)=2) or a_1=2 (gives f(4)=3). Both are allowed slopes (1 and 2 are sunny). So we can set a_1 = 1 (covers (4,2)) or a_1 = 2 (covers (4,3)). Let's decide later.\n\n- For line with v=2: a_2 such that 2 + a_2 = some remaining value in {1,2,3} distinct from the one assigned to v=1. Options: a_2 = -1 (gives 1) but slope -1 not allowed. a_2 = 0 (gives 2) not allowed. a_2 = 1 (gives 3) allowed. So a_2 = 1 gives f(4)=3. So line v=2 with a=1 covers (4,3). But we might already have (4,3) covered by v=1 line if we set a_1=2. So we need to assign distinct values.\n\n- For line with v=4: a_4 such that 4 + a_4 = remaining value in {1,2,3}. Options: a_4 = -3 (gives 1) allowed (slope -3). a_4 = -2 (gives 2) allowed (slope -2). a_4 = -1 (gives 3) not allowed (slope -1). So a_4 can be -3 (covers (4,1)) or -2 (covers (4,2)). So we can assign a_4 = -3 to cover (4,1).\n\nThus we can try to assign:\n\n- v=1 line: a_1 = 2 (covers (4,3)). Then f_1(3)=1, f_1(4)=3, f_1(5)=? f_1(5)=1 + 2*2 = 5 (outside range). So line v=1 with a=2 covers (3,1) and (4,3). It also covers (5,5) which is not n